WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.420
Space pirates make a surprise but welcome return&nbsp;
to the world of "Star Wars" in the Season 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.160
premiere of "The Mandalorian." But something&nbsp;
is very different about these dastardly foes.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.340
The premiere of "The Mandalorian" Season 3 kicks&nbsp;
off the next chapter of Din Djarin's story with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.320
a bang as he and Grogu land on the planet of&nbsp;
Concordia to seek audience with the Armorer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.680
and battle a colossal alien monster along the way.&nbsp;
Branded an apostate by the heretical Mandalorian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:34.020
cult "Children of the Watch," Djarin pleads&nbsp;
with the Armorer for forgiveness and learns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.520
that he must bathe in the "living waters" below&nbsp;
Mandalore to erase his past transgressions.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.200
"This is the way."

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:47.280
From there, Djarin and Grogu set off to&nbsp;
visit some old friends as they prepare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.080
for the desolate wasteland that was once&nbsp;
Mandalore. The duo set off for the Outer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.520
Rim planet of Nevarro to speak with Greef&nbsp;
Karga, the leader of the Bounty Hunter's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.260
Guild and new High Magistrate of Nevarro.&nbsp;
They discover that Karga has transformed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.400
the planet from a criminal hotspot into&nbsp;
a booming hub of trade and industry.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.400
Unfortunately, Djarin's visit is cut short&nbsp;
by the untimely arrival of pirates on Karga's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.500
doorstep who don't seem too thrilled about the new&nbsp;
direction that Nevarro is taking. Karga defeats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.380
the pirate leader, Vane, in a duel. Then Karga&nbsp;
tells Vane to alert Captain Gorian Shard about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.600
Nevarro's latest developments. But who exactly&nbsp;
are these pirates? And who is Gorian Shard?

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.040
Fans of "Star Wars: The Clone Wars" will&nbsp;
know that space pirates played a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:37.500
role during the Clone Wars, specifically the&nbsp;
Weequay pirates led by fan-favorite scoundrel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.720
Hondo Ohnaka who bore the title of "Pirate&nbsp;
King" on Florrum and often found himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.400
at odds with Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan&nbsp;
Kenobi. Despite his criminal background,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.620
Ohnaka would eventually become something&nbsp;
of an antihero, forming a tenuous alliance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.200
with the Galactic Republic and later helping the&nbsp;
fugitive Ezra Bridger during "Star Wars: Rebels."

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.900
Although several of the pirates accompanying&nbsp;
Vane appear to be Weequay, it's worth mentioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.360
that Ohnaka's rule as "Pirate King" came to an&nbsp;
end when the Confederacy shattered his base on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.460
Florrum. This is significant now that Gorian Shard&nbsp;
seems to have claimed that title for himself.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.920
Vane later returns in the episode when he and&nbsp;
his cronies track down Din Djarin and battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.120
him through an asteroid field, eventually&nbsp;
forcing him into the path of the "Pirate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.220
King" Gorian Shard and his immense cruiser.&nbsp;
We get our first look at Shard when he radios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:34.860
Djarin's ship and tells the bounty hunter to&nbsp;
come quietly. The "Pirate King" appears to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:40.560
an entirely new species of alien in the "Star&nbsp;
Wars" universe: a hulking humanoid whose mossy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.060
beard and reptilian face make him look like&nbsp;
an intergalactic counterpart to Swamp Thing.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.460
The fact that Gorian Shard seems to have&nbsp;
taken over from the legendary Hondo Ohnaka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:55.200
as "Pirate King" is extremely telling of&nbsp;
his status among the pirates, though even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.760
more interesting is that his crew seems to be&nbsp;
made up of a swarm of different alien species,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:05.040
not just Weequay. The way Djarin and the pirates&nbsp;
speak about Shard implies that he's become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.960
significant power in the galactic underworld,&nbsp;
perhaps even surpassing the strength of Ohnaka.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:15.120
It's also abundantly clear that Shard and his&nbsp;
pirates now have their sights set on Djarin.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:18.834
"Kid. Never trust a pirate."

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:23.340
Though it remains to be seen how the&nbsp;
mysterious character managed to claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.080
the title of "Pirate King" and how his story&nbsp;
might intertwine with that of Hondo Ohnaka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.120
the return of these space pirates ought to have&nbsp;
plenty of "Clone Wars" fans wondering if Ohnaka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.020
himself might make a surprise appearance&nbsp;
during Season 3 of "The Mandalorian."

